WEBVTT

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:04.068
Most software asks you to trust it.

00:00:04.836 --> 00:00:07.927
This section is the opposite: every claim

00:00:07.988 --> 00:00:11.177
Lolly makes about your content, your data

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:14.204
and its own behaviour is written down here

00:00:14.266 --> 00:00:17.495
with the mechanism that enforces it, so

00:00:17.561 --> 00:00:20.295
you can check rather than believe.

00:00:21.061 --> 00:00:24.163
The internet is optional with Lolly: use

00:00:24.222 --> 00:00:27.645
it when it helps, never surrender control.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:31.414
A font you pick, a place you look up, a

00:00:31.474 --> 00:00:34.097
link you share - things happen online only

00:00:34.157 --> 00:00:35.870
because you asked.

00:00:36.657 --> 00:00:39.123
Nothing you make ever leaves your device

00:00:39.174 --> 00:00:42.440
without your control and informed consent,

00:00:42.528 --> 00:00:44.745
Nobody is listening in.

00:00:45.521 --> 00:00:49.393
Go offline and everything you have works.

00:00:50.192 --> 00:00:52.368
Freedom is sweet.

00:00:53.143 --> 00:00:55.918
The receipts: the Privacy Policy names

00:00:56.027 --> 00:00:59.154
every request the app can ever make, and

00:00:59.216 --> 00:01:02.211
Verify It Yourself shows you how to check

00:01:02.257 --> 00:01:03.469
each one.

00:01:04.604 --> 00:01:07.769
Where did this content come from?

00:01:08.533 --> 00:01:11.102
The media Lolly renders carries Content

00:01:11.161 --> 00:01:14.409
Credentials by default - a signed record

00:01:14.445 --> 00:01:17.670
of what made it, from what and when.

00:01:18.437 --> 00:01:21.287
When a file arrives with a history already

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:24.372
attached, Lolly preserves it rather than

00:01:24.462 --> 00:01:27.544
flattening it, so the chain stays intact

00:01:27.622 --> 00:01:29.220
through an edit.

00:01:29.977 --> 00:01:32.756
Content Credentials - what gets signed,

00:01:32.817 --> 00:01:35.102
what the signature proves and who the

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:36.669
signer is.

00:01:37.429 --> 00:01:39.999
Content Credentials - Engineering - the

00:01:40.085 --> 00:01:44.029
C2PA implementation itself: manifests,

00:01:44.092 --> 00:01:47.294
ingredients, action histories, formats.

00:01:48.081 --> 00:01:52.183
Our AI Stance - where AI is welcome, where

00:01:52.246 --> 00:01:55.468
it is not and why AI-generated content

00:01:55.512 --> 00:01:57.219
declares itself.

00:01:58.343 --> 00:02:01.568
Can I check that for myself?

00:02:02.354 --> 00:02:04.761
You can, and you should - the point of

00:02:04.844 --> 00:02:07.564
provenance is that it does not need our

00:02:07.628 --> 00:02:08.694
word.

00:02:09.478 --> 00:02:12.397
Verify It Yourself - walk the claims on

00:02:12.458 --> 00:02:15.641
this site against a real export, step by

00:02:15.718 --> 00:02:16.744
step.

00:02:17.531 --> 00:02:20.810
Security & Verification - how the code is

00:02:20.882 --> 00:02:23.419
built, signed and checked.

00:02:24.201 --> 00:02:27.106
Threat Model - what Lolly defends against,

00:02:27.171 --> 00:02:30.244
and what it explicitly does not.

00:02:31.002 --> 00:02:33.603
Parser Inventory - every format Lolly

00:02:33.666 --> 00:02:36.212
parses, because parsers are where

00:02:36.318 --> 00:02:39.494
untrusted input meets your device.

00:02:40.286 --> 00:02:43.248
Server Surface - the complete list of what

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:45.494
a server ever sees.

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:49.668
What happens to my data?

00:02:50.474 --> 00:02:53.593
Lolly renders on your device.

00:02:54.368 --> 00:02:57.435
That is not a privacy posture bolted on

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:01.131
afterwards - it is the architecture, and

00:03:01.196 --> 00:03:04.370
it is why most of the usual questions have

00:03:04.464 --> 00:03:06.119
short answers.

00:03:06.875 --> 00:03:09.990
Privacy Policy - what is collected, what

00:03:10.050 --> 00:03:13.144
is not and what leaves your device.

00:03:13.918 --> 00:03:16.818
Data Transfer - moving your work in and

00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.644
out, with nothing held hostage.

00:03:20.417 --> 00:03:23.181
Inclusive Design - who the software is

00:03:23.243 --> 00:03:25.194
built to work for.

00:03:26.335 --> 00:03:28.013
The refusal

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:32.468
Nothing to sell you, nothing to take.

00:03:33.258 --> 00:03:35.655
Four commitments, stated once and

00:03:35.718 --> 00:03:36.943
checkable:

00:03:37.741 --> 00:03:40.568
Free, and it stays free.

00:03:41.336 --> 00:03:43.736
A version that has been released is

00:03:43.811 --> 00:03:47.444
licensed so it can never be taken back.

00:03:48.211 --> 00:03:51.137
The free Lolly always exists, whatever

00:03:51.198 --> 00:03:54.212
happens next - the exact mechanism is on

00:03:54.274 --> 00:03:56.295
How Lolly compares.

00:03:57.069 --> 00:03:58.969
Open source.

00:03:59.745 --> 00:04:02.945
Read it, run it, fork it, keep it.

00:04:03.744 --> 00:04:06.965
Nothing on this page needs to be believed:

00:04:07.027 --> 00:04:09.616
the code is public and the claims are

00:04:09.679 --> 00:04:10.869
checkable.

00:04:11.634 --> 00:04:13.969
Blind by design.

00:04:14.773 --> 00:04:17.568
Lolly reports nothing back.

00:04:18.352 --> 00:04:21.339
Nobody, the makers included, can see who

00:04:21.407 --> 00:04:23.871
runs it or what they make - see the

00:04:23.932 --> 00:04:25.695
Privacy Policy.

00:04:26.443 --> 00:04:29.306
A tool that cannot see you has nothing to

00:04:29.400 --> 00:04:31.045
sell about you.

00:04:31.846 --> 00:04:34.068
Your vote, visible.

00:04:34.868 --> 00:04:37.416
Your work never goes where you have no

00:04:37.526 --> 00:04:38.543
say.

00:04:39.310 --> 00:04:42.008
Anything that touches the internet happens

00:04:42.068 --> 00:04:45.004
because you chose it, at the moment you

00:04:45.065 --> 00:04:48.004
chose it, and the code that keeps that

00:04:48.065 --> 00:04:49.919
promise is open.

00:04:51.056 --> 00:04:53.157
Why this is free

00:04:54.159 --> 00:04:57.268
We built Lolly for ourselves.

00:04:58.068 --> 00:05:01.404
SUSE needed thousands of on-brand files,

00:05:01.473 --> 00:05:04.627
each with its name sealed inside, made

00:05:04.663 --> 00:05:06.978
without handing anything to outside

00:05:07.042 --> 00:05:08.420
services.

00:05:09.211 --> 00:05:12.163
So we built a tool that does all of it on

00:05:12.215 --> 00:05:15.493
the device, and released it as open

00:05:15.604 --> 00:05:18.445
source, like everything else we make.

00:05:19.221 --> 00:05:22.361
We keep maintaining it because we use it

00:05:22.424 --> 00:05:23.769
every day.

00:05:24.544 --> 00:05:27.392
There is no obligation: everything here

00:05:27.455 --> 00:05:29.994
works with or without us.

00:05:30.744 --> 00:05:33.684
If you find a place where these pages and

00:05:33.718 --> 00:05:37.292
the code disagree, the code is the bug -

00:05:37.350 --> 00:05:39.980
and the repository is public so you can

00:05:40.049 --> 00:05:41.995
prove it either way.
